        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We won\u0027t be able to change this later since we can\u0027t update the format of saved information. If we have pad[3] here and use __packed, we could add 3 more bytes of information into the same space. If we don\u0027t use __packed and remove pad[3], then any elements we add to the struct will take more space.\n\nShould I move validate_flags to the end of the struct before pad, since that\u0027s the thing that messes up the alignment?\n\nI doubt we\u0027ll ever modify this struct and there\u0027s a lot of space left in the AP RO flash space, so I\u0027m fine with either. We just need to decide now.",
      "parentUuid": "1db071ba_cfed0035",
