      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need a gbbd specific ap_ro_check_header to validate the saved gbbd information and to have the possiblity of bumping the gbbd version or handling the information differently based on how it was saved later.\n\nAs far as the information included in the gbb descriptor. I\u0027m just worried we\u0027re going to overlook something. I think including the FMAP information helps us do some basic validity checks that the loaded state matches the actual ap ro information. verify_ap_ro_gbb_space just does a memcmp on the gbbd to validate it. Having the gbb and fmap information in addition doesn\u0027t add much overhead.",
